  "narrative": {
   "care_continuity": [
    "National isolation/CTE stock: 813. The source prints no complete national capacity denominator.",
    "Ituri: 473 patients for 978 beds (48.4%); Nord-Kivu: 254 for 220 beds (115.5%); Haut-Uele: 62 for 128 beds (48.4%); Tshopo: 4 for 25 beds (16.0%); Sud-Kivu: 20 patients at a printed 80.0%, which implies 25 beds the edition does not print.",
    "Every printed occupancy percentage agrees with its own printed patient and bed counts this cut. SR115 required two derived corrections (Nord-Kivu and Haut-Uele); SR116 requires none.",
    "Sud-Kivu publishes an isolation block this cut, where it published none in SR115, taking the reporting set to five provinces.",
    "Bas-Uele reports no CTE/CT and no ambulance and publishes no occupancy block; its values remain unset rather than inferred.",
    "The five reporting provinces sum to 813 exactly, matching the printed national stock with no unallocated residual."
   ],
   "challenges": [
    "Alert volume rose 7.3% (1 406 to 1 508), with Sud-Kivu reporting again after publishing no row in SR115, and verification stands at 82.2% (1 240/1 508). Across eight cuts the series has swung +50.2%, -30.3%, +53.1%, -31.3%, +19.6%, -24.1%, -13.6%, +7.3% with no INSP correction to the completeness and time-window question SR109 raised. Treat it as a reporting-coverage artefact, not a transmission signal.",
    "Care capacity: Nord-Kivu is oversaturated for a fifth consecutive cycle at 254 patients against 220 beds, and 101 of those 254 (40%) are still held in facilities that are not CTE. In Ituri the Nizi, Mambasa, Lolwa and Kilo sites are saturated for suspects. At Haut-Uele the Pawa CTE lacks hygiene installations and Isiro lacks space, water and permanent electricity. Tshopo lacks secure blood and runs a limited technical platform. Bas-Uele still has no CTE/CT and no ambulance.",
    "Contact follow-up rose to 88.3% (21 359/24 179), above the 85% threshold, but three provinces sit well below it: Haut-Uele 67.7% (422/623), Tshopo 69.5% (196/282) and Bas-Uele 70.4% (107/152). Sud-Kivu publishes no contact row. INSP attributes the weakness to insufficient teams dedicated to surveillance and contact follow-up, particularly in Bas-Uele.",
    "PoE/PoC report completeness fell to 71.1% (101/142) from 84.6%, with Bas-Uele at 36% (9/25), Tshopo at 39% (7/18) and Sud-Kivu at 55.5% (5/9). Against that, the edition prints 100% strategic-point functionality in every province, where SR115 printed 9.1% for Ituri and 31.8% nationally. A jump that large in one cut, while report completeness is falling, is more consistent with a change in what is counted than with a restored network."
   ],
   "highlights": [
    "DRC: 6757 confirmed and 3267 confirmed deaths.",
    "24h: 71 confirmations and 41 deaths (31 community, 10 intra-CTE).",
    "Footprint: 61/151 health zones across six provinces; no new zone this cut.",
    "Nord-Kivu is over isolation capacity for a fifth consecutive cut (254 patients, 220 beds)."
   ]
  },
